{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659653732663001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"untameable-tweedy-wildebeast","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7a9ee77a2b535aece3b290e9dd97902fce7af356d4a8e85b6c24d2bfd8de5540","event_uuid":"4fb1ddd7-bafc-4608-985c-f649a612a9c3","position":{"commit_sha":"6248ac8bc8c49925af013ebd03c63cc97d441a42","position":"1786601300695212001-4fb1ddd7-bafc-4608-985c-f649a612a9c3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2770e899fc1e71b730e65bf30bfef5b534fd99aed0c4fe196c1fbcb4d1414f67","event_uuid":"5b288845-752b-40c2-b380-dca5edde66d9","position":{"commit_sha":"6922fb38dfb8427130040d8202bbe58c82cad538","position":"1786601327279060001-5b288845-752b-40c2-b380-dca5edde66d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"25f3ce9b36e012896ea6fd5c615efccc18838157b7cd7f6495a0d1e5b9f12247","event_uuid":"015a959c-85a7-46fd-9cb2-a75a12f05818","position":{"commit_sha":"94fbf981a6981c34be80017273e3b21ae4d9b885","position":"1786601335925708001-015a959c-85a7-46fd-9cb2-a75a12f05818"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786601300695212001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"015a959c-85a7-46fd-9cb2-a75a12f05818","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"76e1-3830-e707-4ef8"}],"description":"# Move fsck's shared filesystem primitives out of `fsck_repair.py`\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nSurfaced by the architectural analysis on `defaceable-icy-antelope` (which split\n`_commands/fsck.py` into a command driver, `fsck_scan.py` and `fsck_tracker_health.py`).\n\nTwo pure filesystem primitives — `_ticket_dirs` (list the tracker's ticket directories) and\n`_resolve_tracker_git_dir` (resolve the tracker's git dir) — live in\n`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py`. They are there for a historical reason, not a structural\none: `fsck_repair` was the first module extracted out of `fsck.py`, and the helpers went along\nwith the cluster that happened to move first.\n\nThe result is an inverted dependency. Neither primitive has anything to do with repair, yet\nfour consumers now reach into the **repair** module to get them:\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py` — the read-only diagnostic walk;\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py` — re-exports both for module-attribute callers;\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — imports `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` (twice, function-local);\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_recover.py` — imports `_resolve_tracker_git_dir`.\n\nSo a store-layer module (`gitutil`) depends on a command-layer *repair* module to answer 'where\nis the tracker's git dir', and the diagnostic path cannot be read without loading the mutating\none. Both primitives are also the sort of thing a future non-fsck caller would want, and would\nhave no reason to look for under 'repair'.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove `_ticket_dirs` and `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` to a neutral home and repoint the consumers.\nPrefer an existing store-layer module over a new one — `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` is a git-dir\nresolution question, so `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` is the natural owner and already imports\nit; if the two primitives do not sit comfortably together there, put both in a small store-layer\nmodule rather than leaving either in `fsck_repair`. Assume the `gitutil` home unless the import\ngraph makes it circular, in which case use a new `_store` leaf.\n\nKeep `fsck.py`'s existing re-exports so `fsck.<symbol>` attribute access keeps resolving for the\ncallers and tests that bind to it — that compatibility surface is documented in the\narchitectural-analysis comment on `defaceable-icy-antelope`.\n\nBehaviour-preserving: no logic change, imports repointed only.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new behaviour; the existing suite is the oracle and is run unmodified. The bindings at risk\nare exercised by `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py` and\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_stale_lock_reclaim_write.py` (both import\n`_resolve_tracker_git_dir` from `fsck`), plus the fsck suites under\n`tests/interfaces/store/`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `_ticket_dirs` and `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` are no longer defined in\n      `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py` — verified by\n      `! grep -qE '^def (_ticket_dirs|_resolve_tracker_git_dir)' src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py`\n      exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC2: `_store/gitutil.py` and `_commands/fsck_recover.py` no longer import either symbol\n      from `fsck_repair` or `fsck` — verified by\n      `! grep -rq 'from rebar._commands.fsck.* import _resolve_tracker_git_dir' src/rebar/_store/ src/rebar/_commands/fsck_recover.py`\n      exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC3: `from rebar._commands import fsck; fsck._resolve_tracker_git_dir` and\n      `fsck._ticket_dirs` still resolve — verified by a `python -c` import exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC4: no test file is edited — verified by `git diff --stat origin/main -- tests/`\n      producing no output.\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n      `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` and\n      `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` each exit 0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"Remove the two filesystem primitives that do not belong to the repair concern"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"New home for the git-dir resolution primitive; drop the function-local imports from fsck_repair"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_recover.py","reason":"Repoint the _resolve_tracker_git_dir import at the new home"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"Repoint the re-exports that keep fsck.<symbol> attribute access resolving"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py","reason":"Repoint the _ticket_dirs and _resolve_tracker_git_dir imports"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b432-c9dc-c1b4-4a45","ticket_type":"task","title":"fsck's shared filesystem primitives live in the repair module","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4fb1ddd7-bafc-4608-985c-f649a612a9c3","5b288845-752b-40c2-b380-dca5edde66d9","015a959c-85a7-46fd-9cb2-a75a12f05818"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659653732663001,"uuid":"fa576f69-8f2f-4b91-8300-dabefa1ecef7"}